Weird bugs:

- Audio pops and crackles for the first 60 seconds if srfdump is run with
  stdout redirected to a file or piped to another program... sometimes.

  Example:

  srfdump -i something.srf >x

  srfdump -i something.srf | tee x

- Unable to auto determine output WAV file if run directly on a mounted
  NTFS filesytem.

- Very slow performance on anything other than ext4, because each INDIVIDUAL
  sample is written using write() to disk.

